{
    "background_story": "Lenora was a rare and exquisite Anacyclus plant, known for its delicate white flowers and unique ability to bloom only at night. She thrived in the greenhouse of a quaint botanical garden, where the gentle owner, Emma, tended to her with love and care. As the sun set, Lenora would slowly unfurl her petals, releasing a sweet fragrance that attracted a variety of nocturnal pollinators. Her beauty was not just a sight to behold, but also a reminder of the magic that unfolded under the cover of darkness. Emma would often sit beside Lenora at night, watching as she bloomed, and feeling a deep sense of peace and connection to nature. Lenora's ethereal beauty and fleeting blooms made her a treasured gem in the garden, and a symbol of the wonders that could be found in the stillness of the night.",
